9591568,2024-07-24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Card was charged for something you did not purchase with the card,"( Note : I've attached a full explanation with screenshots of correspondence to this complaint. I am copying the text portion of the situation summary here, but please view the attached document for the full explanation with evidence. ) To whom it may concern, Here is an explanation of all the events related to the recent scam I was unfortunately involved in, in hopes that Wells Fargo could help me successfully dispute the fraudulent {$1000.00} charge. 
On XX/XX/XXXX, while I was at my friends wedding, I received a missed call about my XXXX  services ( wifi ) ending soon. I was told I would need to restart my services or else they would be cut. I had told XXXX  at the start of my services XX/XX/XXXX that I only need wifi for a year, so the timing matched up in my mind. In addition, the scam agent knew my name, address, and last XXXX of my credit card, which unfortunately made him appear more credible to me. I was told that XXXX was partnering with XXXX to give a discount for customers for the next XXXX  months, as long as payment was made upfront with a XXXX gift card. I unfortunately did not think too hard about this suspicious-sounding discount. Attached are the initial calls and invoice I was sent from these scammers. They told me they would charge me {$1.00} as a holding amount for this discount, which is the {$1.00} charge on XX/XX/XXXX I later disputed with Wells Fargo. 
The next morning, XX/XX/XXXX, I went and bought the XXXX gift card and paid it to the scammers, as I had been instructed under the pretense of a wifi-service discount. Later that day, I received a missed call from the scammers saying I needed to go buy another gift card from XXXX or XXXX as the XXXX  store I bought my original gift card from had a system shutdown and the gift card payment did not go through. Attached is my call back to that number where I tried to figure out what happened. Notice how this number matches up with the number at the bottom of the invoice. I was told that I had XXXX  days to make the payment or else my discount would be void, but that XXXX would refund my {$300.00} and send me an additional {$100.00} for the inconvenience. 
At this point, it became clear to me that I fell for a scam so I immediately blocked these numbers. I called Wells Fargo explaining the situation, as I felt my credit card had been compromised given the scammers knew a lot of my information ( below is the record of my phone call ). Wells Fargo cancelled my XXXX card and sent me a new one. They also helped me open a dispute for the {$300.00} XXXX  gift card I bought, even though I knew it would not ultimately be successful ( I was later called by their department where I gave my permission to close the dispute for this {$300.00} charge for the XXXX  gift card ). I felt at this point that the rest of my money would be secure. 
On XX/XX/XXXX, I received several texts from the scammers telling me that I needed to activate my promotion in order to receive my {$400.00} refund. I ignored these texts and blocked these numbers. The next day XX/XX/XXXX, however, I received XXXX texts saying I was being charged {$1000.00} due to not following through with the payment. I then received an official email from XXXX saying that I paid {$1000.00} via my XXXX card with Automated Agent. The scammers sent a follow-up text confirming that I had been charged {$1000.00}. I was extremely confused how the scammers could still use my XXXX card given it had been cancelled by Wells Fargo on XX/XX/XXXX. I also received a call from Wells Fargo regarding this payment, as it had triggered a suspicious activity alert. I called back immediately to alert Wells Fargo that I was NOT the one who made this payment and was told that the fraud team would help me handle it. At this point, my newly mailed credit card was again cancelled, and a new one was sent. 
