9624961,2024-07-26,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX, TX XXXX Subject : Second Request for Credit Information Correction - Non-Compliance with 15 U.S. Code 1666b and Other FCRA Provisions I am writing to follow up on my previous letter dated [ XX/XX/XXXX ], in which I requested the correction of inaccurate information on my credit report regarding incorrectly reported late payments on my credit card, auto loan, and/or mortgage account. Account Name : XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX Re : Account # XXXX. To date, I have not received confirmation of the correction nor observed any changes in my credit report. 

As stated in my previous correspondence, according to 15 U.S. Code 1666b, creditors must send periodic statements, including all information required by section 1637 ( b ), at least 21 days before the payment due date. This requirement ensures that consumers have sufficient time to receive, review, and make necessary payments without being unfairly penalized for late payments. 

