Dear, CAPITOL ONE BANK I am writing to inform you about Section 602 of the Fair Credit Reporting Act, as outlined in 15 U.S. Code 1681. This section addresses the permissible purposes for which consumer reporting agencies may furnish consumer reports.

Under Section 602, consumer reporting agencies are only allowed to provide consumer reports to entities that have a legitimate business need for the information. These permissible purposes include evaluating a consumer 's creditworthiness, making decisions regarding credit or insurance applications, and conducting employment background checks.

